     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Sun, 13 Sep 2020 at 11:35, Franziska Merle Willems &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">franzisk...@uni-tuebingen.de</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;display:inline\">Dear all,</span><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Firstly thanks for your great work on INLA! I just started using it for my analysis and it is just what I needed and I enjoy it a lot.</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">My question is: How can I implement random slopes in a spde-model in Inla?. </div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">In my analysis I have fixed effects, random effects (for Species) and a SPDE spatial random effect. (I copied Species to be able to use it twice).So my model formula would look something like this:</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div><font face=\"Courier\">f &lt;- y ~ -1 + Intercept + Temperature + other_Covariates + </font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\">        f(Species, model = &quot;iid&quot;) +                # Random Intercept for Species</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\">        f(Species2, Temperature, model = &quot;iid&quot;) +  # Random Slope for Species</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\">        f(w, model = spde) </font>                                                    <font face=\"Courier\"># Spatial random effect</font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">What I haven’t been able to figure out is how to adapt the stack. The version with just the random intercepts for Species works fine and the stack for that looks like this: </div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div><font face=\"Courier\">Stack &lt;- inla.stack( </font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\">            tag = &quot;Fit&quot;,</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\">            data = list(y = D$DOY),            # Response variable</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>          A = list(1, 1, A_spde, 1),   # </font><span style=\"font-family:Courier\">A_spde = from </span><font face=\"Courier\">inla.spde.make.A()</font><span style=\"font-family:Courier\">    </span></div><div><font face=\"Courier\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>          effects = list(   </font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>              Intercept = rep(1, N),</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>              X = X,                   # Matrix with covariates</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>              w = w,                   # Spatial component from spde</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>              Species = D.ce$Species   # Random intercept for Species</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>              ))</font></div></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12p